A||||2||batboy||Door panel is loose
Z||000000||batboy||06-30-99||06:31 PM||||The inner driver's door panel keeps pulling out and gapping at the top towards the front near the mirror adjuster knob. Anyone else ever had this problem? I'm guessing I have to remove the door panel to fix it. Once it's off though, what do I look for or do? Also, the mirror adjuster knob sticks up higher than it should. Are these two problems related?
Z||000001||theogre||06-30-99||07:17 PM||||The top of the pannel is not well supported and warps. The problems are related.<p>Exactly how to fix a major warp I don't know yet. My door is in pretty good shape so I don't want to fool with it til I have too.<p>The Mirror control is also not well suported, and it has torq from the cables pulling at it. I have to fix mine...... I have seen the back side of a panel that was off.... I think a couple flat washers, with large outside diameters, are all that needs. Something to spread out the load on the nuts. There's nothing on the studs from the factory but the nuts, and they are pretty small.
Z||000002||batboy||06-30-99||07:55 PM||||Thanks Ogre, that gives me an idea what I'm up against. I'm half tempted to disconnect the mirror adjusting cable. I'm the only one who drives my Fiero and I don't plan on selling it any time soon. I've never had to adjust the mirror except once when I first bought it. I can always roll the window down and adjust it manually in the "old fashion" way.
